  "about": "The contract of the English phonetic key (en-rules). 'collide' groups must all get the same key; 'differ' pairs must get different keys; 'known_shared' pairs are opposite-sex first names that are the same sound in English and that no rule can separate (the sex rule of lot 2 bis lists them instead of hiding them); 'observe' names are only printed. Add a row, run: cargo test --test knowledge_names -- --nocapture. A collision is a hint to the resolver (a 'did you mean'), never a merge. Names come from public lists of surnames and first names (US Census 2010, US SSA); none is a real person's record. 'false_friends' are pairs the owner judged to be two different names that the key still cannot separate (kept so that the limit is measured, and so that a rule that separates them is noticed).",
